{{Otheruses|Qian}} {{Bagua}} '''Qian''' (乾) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|qq=draft}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☰'''}} and consists of three Yang (⚊) {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|qq=draft}}. It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|qq=draft}}, known as {{ill|Qian as Heaven|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian為天|qq=draft}}, consisting of Qian below and Qian above.
== Trigram Symbolism == Qian symbolizes heaven, strength, horses, the head, the father, and the sovereign. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft}}, it represents the {{ill|northwest|ja|北西|qq=draft}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=draft}} system, Qian is associated with {{ill|Jia (Heavenly Stem)|ja|甲|1=Kinoe (甲)|qq=draft}}, the Wood element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=draft}}, and the {{ill|east|ja|東|qq=draft}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=draft}}. Alternatively, it can also correspond to {{ill|Ren (Heavenly Stem)|ja|壬|1=Mizunoe (壬)|qq=draft}}, the Water element, and the {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=draft}}. The Earthly Branches {{ill|Xu (戌)|ja|戌|1=Dog (zodiac)|lt=Dog (戌)|qq=draft}} and {{ill|Hai (亥)|ja|亥|1=Pig (zodiac)|lt=Pig (亥)|qq=draft}} are associated with emotions such as crying, joy, happiness, and friendship.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft}}, Qian corresponds to the {{ill|northwest|ja|北西|qq=draft}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=draft}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt\=Dui (☱)|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=draft}}, and Qian (乾)—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Xu (戌)|ja|戌|1=Dog (zodiac)|lt=Dog (戌)|qq=draft}} (*inu*) and {{ill|Hai (亥)|ja|亥|1=Pig (zodiac)|lt=Pig (亥)|qq=draft}} (*i*), Qian is also read as *Inui* (いぬい).
