== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft|qq=}}, Qian corresponds to the {{ill|northwest|ja|北西|qq=draft|qq=}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=draft|qq=}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|2=ja|3=兌|4=zh-yue|5=兌卦|6=ko|7=태 (괘)|8=fr|9=Duì|10=nl|11=Meer (trigram)|12=pt|13=Duì (I Ching)|14=zh-min-nan|15=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt\=Dui (☱)|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=draft|qq=}}, and Qian (乾)—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Xu (戌)|ja|戌|1=Dog (zodiac)|lt=Dog (戌)|qq=draft|qq=}} (*inu*) and {{ill|Hai (亥)|ja|亥|1=Pig (zodiac)|lt=Pig (亥)|qq=draft|qq=}} (*i*), Qian is also read as *Inui* (いぬい).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=draft|qq=}}, Qian is the first in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing {{ill|south|ja|南|qq=draft|qq=}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the extreme of Yang.
