In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Na Jia|qq=}} system, Qian is associated with {{ill|Jia (Heavenly Stem)|ja|甲|1=Kinoe (甲)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jia (Heavenly Stem)|13=User:Immanuelle/Kinoe (甲)|qq=}}, the Wood element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|13=User:Immanuelle/Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|qq=}}, and the {{ill|east|ja|東|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/east|qq=}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Five Directions|qq=}}. Alternatively, it can also correspond to {{ill|Ren (Heavenly Stem)|ja|壬|1=Mizunoe (壬)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ren (Heavenly Stem)|13=User:Immanuelle/Mizunoe (壬)|qq=}}, the Water element, and the {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/north|qq=}}. The Earthly Branches {{ill|Xu (戌)|ja|戌|1=Dog (zodiac)|lt=Dog (戌)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xu (戌)|13=User:Immanuelle/Dog (zodiac)|qq=}} and {{ill|Hai (亥)|ja|亥|1=Pig (zodiac)|lt=Pig (亥)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hai (亥)|13=User:Immanuelle/Pig (zodiac)|qq=}} are associated with emotions such as crying, joy, happiness, and friendship.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/cardinal direction|qq=}}, Qian corresponds to the {{ill|northwest|ja|北西|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/northwest|qq=}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Earthly Branches|qq=}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kan|13=User:Immanuelle/Kan (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gen|13=User:Immanuelle/Gen (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Zhen|13=User:Immanuelle/Zhen (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xun|13=User:Immanuelle/Xun (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Li|13=User:Immanuelle/Li (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|2=ja|3=坤|lt=Kun (坤)|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kun|13=User:Immanuelle/Kun (Bagua)|qq=}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|2=ja|3=兌|4=zh-yue|5=兌卦|6=ko|7=태 (괘)|8=fr|9=Duì|10=nl|11=Meer (trigram)|12=pt|13=Duì (I Ching)|14=zh-min-nan|15=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt\=Dui (☱)|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Dui|13=User:Immanuelle/Dui (Bagua)|qq=}}, and Qian (乾)—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Xu (戌)|ja|戌|1=Dog (zodiac)|lt=Dog (戌)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Xu (戌)|13=User:Immanuelle/Dog (zodiac)|qq=}} (*inu*) and {{ill|Hai (亥)|ja|亥|1=Pig (zodiac)|lt=Pig (亥)|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hai (亥)|13=User:Immanuelle/Pig (zodiac)|qq=}} (*i*), Qian is also read as *Inui* (いぬい).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|qq=}}, Qian is the first in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing {{ill|south|ja|南|qq=draft|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/south|qq=}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the extreme of Yang.
